From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: playportdev <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:28:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 85/85] ntdll: steer reserve-only arenas out of the guest
 window from the first one

The valve that moves reserve-only 32 MB to 1 GB reserves above the furniture
ceiling armed only at 8 GB reserved or once ios_va_pressure was latched, and
the latch came from a boot-time scan grinding through iOS's low VA, which
happened on some launches and not others. On the others Death's Door's first
14 x 512 MB reserves (7 GB) went into the 16 GB guest window and filled it.
With the grind gone (a 4 GB floor is no constraint) no launch would latch it
early.

Now every such reserve is first placed in [0x7400000000, ios_spill_cap). The
FEX-band fallback and the dead-thread reclaim keep the old arming, so the
band, where every FEX thread's rpmalloc spans must fit, is not used sooner.
When that range is held (The Witcher 3's jumbo hold) the reserve takes the
normal path, as before. [steer] lines say armed=always for these.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-06-guest-va-exhaustion.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 18 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 7f6e50f..be3f535 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -19053,10 +19053,18 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtAllocateVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *ret, ULONG_PTR z
              * a steer that cannot be served is still never worse than not
              * steering. The 1GB ceiling stays: >=1GB reserves are PartitionAlloc
              * pool business and go through the jumbo path above. */
+            /* Playport: steer from the first reserve, into [0x7400000000,
+             * ios_spill_cap) only, and arm the FEX-band fallback and the reclaim
+             * as before (8 GB reserved, or va-pressure). Gated on pressure alone,
+             * the first 8 GB of these reserves went into the 16 GB guest window
+             * unless a boot-time scan had happened to grind first: Death's Door's
+             * 14 x 512 MB filled it on the launches where none had (evidence
+             * 2026-10-06-guest-va-exhaustion.md), and with that grind gone (a
+             * 4 GB floor is no constraint) no launch would latch early. */
+            int steer_armed = (ios_bigres_reserved_total > (8ull << 30) || ios_va_pressure);
             if (!ios_steered
                 && !*ret && !limit && (type & MEM_RESERVE) && !(type & MEM_COMMIT)
-                && *size_ptr >= 0x2000000 && *size_ptr < 0x40000000
-                && (ios_bigres_reserved_total > (8ull << 30) || ios_va_pressure))
+                && *size_ptr >= 0x2000000 && *size_ptr < 0x40000000)
             {
                 SIZE_T want = *size_ptr;
                 void *saved = *ret;
@@ -19108,7 +19116,7 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtAllocateVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *ret, ULONG_PTR z
                  * the reserve count went 27 -> 55 (28160MB) and BOTH the steer slot and
                  * furniture reported va-scan FAILED maxgap=0 before the NULL deref.
                  * Fall back to the other slot. That doubles steer capacity to ~32GB. */
-                if (sst)
+                if (sst && steer_armed)
                 {
                     *ret = saved; *size_ptr = want;
                     sst = allocate_virtual_memory( ret, size_ptr, type, protect,
@@ -19119,7 +19127,7 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtAllocateVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *ret, ULONG_PTR z
                  * have since exited, then retry once. This is what makes the steer
                  * region sustainable: the reserves leak per-thread, so without this any
                  * fixed capacity is exhausted by a long enough run. */
-                if (sst && ios_steer_reclaim_dead())
+                if (sst && steer_armed && ios_steer_reclaim_dead())
                 {
                     *ret = saved; *size_ptr = want;
                     sst = allocate_virtual_memory( ret, size_ptr, type, protect,
@@ -19151,7 +19159,7 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtAllocateVirtualMemory( HANDLE process, PVOID *ret, ULONG_PTR z
                     dprintf(2, "[steer] #%u size=0x%lx reserved_total=%lluMB armed=%s -> %s %p\n",
                             steer_n, (unsigned long)want,
                             (unsigned long long)(ios_bigres_reserved_total >> 20),
-                            ios_va_pressure ? "va-pressure" : "8GB-total",
+                            !steer_armed ? "always" : ios_va_pressure ? "va-pressure" : "8GB-total",
                             sst ? "FAILED, falling back" : "above ceiling", *ret);
                 }
                 if (!sst) { st = sst; ios_steered = 1; }
